 for families. The result is put into context with the Nielsen realisation problem for aspherical manifolds, and we give a unifying account of different formulations of that problem, made possible by the same methods.\nL17: Comments:  | 7 pages, comments welcome\nL18: Subjects:  | Geometric Topology (math.GT); Algebraic Topology (math.AT)\nL19: Report number:  | MPIM-Bonn-2025\nL20: Cite as:  | cite8†arXiv:2510.21550 [math.GT]\nL21:    | (or cite9†arXiv:2510.21550v1 [math.GT] for this version)\nL22:    | cite10†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2510.21550†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Christian Kremer [cite11†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Fri, 24 Oct 2025 15:09:07 UTC (14 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Borel actions in nonpositively curved geometry and the Nielsen realisation problem, by Christian Kremer\nL33: \nL34:   * cite6†View PDF L35:   * cite7†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite12†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite13†view license†creativecommons.org L39: ### Current browse context:\nL40: \nL41: math.GT\nL42: \nL43: cite14†< prev |   cite15†next > L44: \nL45: cite16†new | cite17†recent | cite18†2025-10 L46: \nL47: Change to browse by:\nL48: \nL49: cite19†math L50: cite20†math.AT L51: \nL52: ### References & Citations\nL53: \nL54:   * cite21†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L55:   * cite22†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L56:   * cite23†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L57: \nL58: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL59: \nL60: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL61: \nL62: [Button: ×]\nL63: \nL64: loading...\nL65: \nL66: Data provided by:\nL67: \nL68: ### Bookmark\nL69: \nL70: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL71: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL72: \nL73: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL74: \nL75: Bibliographic Explorer (cite24†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL76